description:
The migration to Theseus v0.2.x (PR #3962) renamed the caller workflows and contexts, but kept several oracle names to limit the diff and avoid breaking live infrastructure:
- the policy file `.github/oracle-reviewers.yml`, passed via `policy_path`;
- the GitHub environment `oracle` and its `ORACLE_*` secrets, mapped to `REVIEW_*` by name;
- the tailnet tag `tag:oracle-ci`;
- the local-review state directory `local-oracle`;
- scripts such as `scripts/oracle_local_review.py` and `_project/scripts/oracle_gateway_host.sh`;
- docs `docs/internal/oracle-review-v2.md` and `docs/internal/oracle-gateway-host.md`;
- the still-required legacy context `oracle-gate`.

Theseus v0.2.2 removes its `legacy.py` mirror and its legacy-name reading, so BenchBox must stop depending on `oracle-gate` and the `/oracle-review` and `Stand-in oracle` command forms before it re-locks to v0.2.2.
